    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i need some help with a calculation for a loft i'm adding to a house here in oregon. i'm using a douglas fir beam for the main span. the span is gonna be 14 feet. i'm planning on a live load of 30 psf and a dead load of 15 psf. can you help me figure out what size beam i'm gonna need to keep deflection within L/360?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! For a 14-foot span using Douglas Fir, a common choice is an I-beam or L-beam. Considering a combined live and dead load of 45 psf, you'd likely need a beam around 6x16 and 8 inches deep to keep deflection within L/360. It's always best to consult with a structural engineer for the final sizing and confirmation.",
